<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for claude-google, a private read-only tool for my own Google accounts.">
	<article>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="post-meta">Effective {effective} · claude-google</p>

		<p>This page covers claude-google, a small tool I wrote to read my own Google accounts. It is not offered to anyone else, and only accounts I own are allowed to sign in to it.</p>

		<h2>The limits</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Read-only. It asks Google for read access to Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive, and for nothing else. It cannot send, delete, share or change anything.</li>
			<li>It runs on my own computer. Sign-in credentials stay in the macOS Keychain. There is no server and no database holding your data or mine.</li>
			<li>Nothing it reads is sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>What it does</h2>
		<p>It lets me search and read my own mail, calendar and files in two places: a reading digest that gathers newsletters I subscribe to, and Claude, Anthropic's assistant, when I ask a question about my own accounts. Text it reads goes to Anthropic only to answer those requests or to rank my reading list, and Anthropic handles it under <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">its privacy policy</a>.</p>

		<h2>Google user data</h2>
		<p>claude-google's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>

		<h2>Removing access</h2>
		<p>Access can be revoked at any time from <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a>. Questions go to <a href="mailto:barrett@bryansoron.ca">barrett@bryansoron.ca</a>.</p>
	</article>
</Base>
